    "observations": [
      "Direct RGB restores sharp check corners and thin hummingbird/dragonfly details; it also restores false stripes, dots and fine speckle on printed paper.",
      "Native dinosaur and star candidates retain recognizable motifs with errors 1.29% and 0.84%, but fail feature checks on small isolated components near the right or bottom crop edge. The checks remain enforced.",
      "Mother/child loses a substantial interior detail in fitting despite preserving it in the native mask. Repeated hearts exceed the 3% image-error limit at 3.165625%. All four losses have identical crops to their baseline.",
      "The nativity and red/black girl with bird remain search failures even with visually recognizable masks. The native results do not identify a single causal search branch.",
      "The reflective-building and basket proposals still crop the wrong regions; changing classification does not repair them. All six missing proposals remain unresolved.",
      "Every method still treats the printed central flower as a cutting motif and passes its own mask checks. Self-mask fit success is not recovery of the actual weave.",
      "Neutralized query deviation still has the highest self-mask pass count, but includes the wrong basket and retains rounded-corner/detailed-shape problems. It is not automatically adopted."
    ]
  },
